(r/'README_DOCX.md').write_text('''# Source DOCX checkpoint — P-VCNA-003\n\n64 independent native editable Word files (25 Table, 2 Figure, 37 Listing), 64 Locator Maps and 77 rendered pages are persisted. The source output type controls the folder; two Table-labelled shells retain listing structures. Both Figures retain their actual textual specification boxes. No plotted results, simulated data, copied layout-only outputs or target-study adaptation were generated.\n\nEach file contains real collapsed START/END bookmarks and precise occurrence bookmarks. Actual Word XML was checked for names/IDs, existence, order, containment, source text and hash. All 73 physical footnotes and all substantive source/programming notes are visible editable body content inside the shell boundary. No source Word endnotes were supplied (input is PDF).\n\n5,682 occurrences have verified actual bookmarks. 300 corporate source-header/form-footer occurrences are consistently excluded from shell content and remain in source records/maps with null locators. Corporate logos are excluded as wrappers. Actual source study/date/path/Page x/y placeholders are retained. The validator reports wrapper occurrences once for each structure/map representation (600 review warnings), not 600 missing clinical elements.\n\nAll 77 final rendered page images were viewed by the executing agent, with source-region comparison. No missing/extra rendered non-whitespace characters or out-of-page text was detected; no visible clipping or overlap was observed. Native Word text flow and line lengths are not a pixel-identical PDF facsimile.\n\n57 IDs pass the current representation review; 7 source/fine-structure issues remain pending and are listed in README_Structure.md and the per-ID issue records. Their DOCX files exist and preserve the original source, including source defects, without guessing corrections. Footnote semantic interpretation remains for metadata. Independent visual/clinical QA is not_run and human approval is pending.\n\nTwo source programming-note continuation lines were initially classified as titles. They were corrected without changing original text, recorded in qa/Corrections_Log.json, and the affected DOCX/maps/hashes were regenerated and re-rendered.\n\nThis is a stage-3 checkpoint, not a completed or approved searchable library. Stage 4 metadata and stage 5 final QA have not been run.\n''')
